# Software Engineering Tasks

- Use `task_type = "software_engineering"`,
  `reward_type = "multi_deterministic_rubrics"`, and the narrowest software
  domain. Start brand-new tasks from the `software-engineering` starter.
- Prefer the secure single-image `/tmp/output/repo` contract. Add capability
  sections/services only when workspace lifecycle or live topology is essential.
- Graders declare `TASK = RubricTask(...)` with
  `WorkspaceArtifact("repo", reject_native_payloads=True)`.
- Candidate code runs only through `context.run_candidate` or
  `run_candidate_suite`; trusted references run before candidate code.
- Keep `allow_internet = false`, main unprivileged, hidden fixtures root-only,
  and verifier isolated from agent networks/volumes/dependencies.
- Explicit services require exactly one main; verifier requires explicit
  `[result]`; images are local-build or digest pinned; named volumes only.
- Captures are ordered/atomic/bounded; artifacts are service-qualified and
  byte/file/depth bounded; Taiga service tasks use a trusted outer capsule.
- Taiga MCP uses only the audited capsule service-DNS SSE proxy.
- Include no-op/unchanged-starter and task-specific attack regressions.
- Acceptance requires every trusted CI check green and Boreal aggregate
  `<= 0.4` across valid attempts.

Read `software-engineering-tasks`, `service-capsule-tasks`,
`reward-hacking-security`, and `docs/SOFTWARE_ENGINEERING_FRAMEWORK.md`.
